  "body": "### What is the issue with the HTML Standard?\n\nI just noticed that many statements (26) in the spec say something like `Let <var>foo</var> be 0`.\n\nWe also have 5 statements which say `Let <var>foo</var> be zero.`.\n\nThis feels a little inconsistent. Is there good justification for these 5 \"zero\"s? Should we refactor them to say \"0\"?",
